bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    closure_views_miss_calls_nested_in_call_args_2026_11_07, 1, "2026-11-08 p3-dedupe: source implementation is present: node_view_walk recursively visits flat_expr_child_exprs, whose EXPR_CALL/EXPR_METHOD_CALL arm includes both the callee and every argument. Added a discriminating str(int(x) + 1) regression requiring two call views with exact argument/name spans. Status fix-implemented-verification-pending: the deployed seed cannot execute it because windows_redirected_process.spl uses newer block-form @when syntax; no runtime pass or fixed mark is claimed."
    closure_views_miss_calls_nested_in_call_args_2026_11_07, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep7: probe enumerated 20 nested-call shapes - every shape yields an anchored call view at tip; end-to-end code_entry refactor --closure matched all 4/4 nested int sites (the doc's 13-site class, offsets 30/82/129/143). Root cause (historical): the pure-Simple parser left callees of calls nested in call args spanless, so name anchoring never fired, name_start stayed -1, and closure_runner.spl:_rename_targets dropped them; the textual callee-name recovery at node_view_walk.spl:228-239 (303e893e0d7, ancestor of HEAD) fixed it. Specs extended: node_view_walk_spec +54 (nested-callee anchoring across binary-arg/index-arg/method-arg/direct-arg shapes + pre-order visit order) 9/9; closure_runner_spec +14 (rename reaches calls only from nested args) 9/9; neighbours bound_late_cast_registry 5/5, dummy_accessor_fix 10/10, fix_engine 7/7, newunit_deprecation_fix 10/10, rewriter_atomic_write_contract 2/2, str_brace001_fix 15/15. Residual: the sibling int(text)-single-char JIT hazard row remains open per the audit doc. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/tools/fix/node_view_walk_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/tools/fix/closure_runner_spec.spl"

